{{also|Software}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|soft|-ware|id2=substance, kind, or use}}, by contrast with {{m|en|hardware||the computer itself}}. {{coin|en|in=1958|John Tukey|nobycat=1|w=-}}.<ref>"[https://www.economist.com/science-and-technology/2000/06/01/how-software-got-its-name]", ''[https://www.economist.com/science-and-technology/2000/06/01/how-software-got-its-name How software got its name],'' 2000, the Economist</ref><ref>"[https://www.nytimes.com/2000/07/28/us/john-tukey-85-statistician-coined-the-word-software.html]",''[https://www.nytimes.com/2000/07/28/us/john-tukey-85-statistician-coined-the-word-software.html John Tukey, 85, Statistician; Coined the Word 'Software']'', 2000, The New York Times</ref>

